From: CDNCA edge runtime maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] QUIC: route new and established connections across reload

Backport the complete eBPF QUIC dispatch model to the OpenResty-pinned Nginx
1.27.1 source.  Each reuseport group keeps separate sockets for accepting new
connections and serving established connections.  New Initial packets route
only to the active master generation while connection-ID entries keep existing
connections on their draining workers.

This replaces the insufficient listener-only workaround: closing non-owning
socket copies cannot prevent the kernel from hashing a fresh Initial packet to
the old worker socket that must remain open for established connections.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/nginx/nginx/issues/425
Upstream Nginx proposal: https://github.com/nginx/nginx/pull/1219
Reference implementation:
https://github.com/webserver-llc/angie/commit/4b527f5087923c7da54c301648840221fa1d727d

Included Nginx proposal commits are limited to the reload dispatcher, inherited
map error handling, removal of a generated build artifact, and IPv6 worker
socket handling.  Unrelated QUIC payload-size changes are intentionally omitted.

